        "original_id": "0957c14c-7512-593c-939f-b5c5b10a632c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keith Scholey, Alastair Fothergill\n- Films: Bears, Aliens of the Deep, African Cats\n- Organizations: Disneynature, Walden Media, Walt Disney Pictures, BBC, BBC Natural History Unit\n- TV Series: Big Cat Diary\n- Places: Alaska\n\nFacts:\n- In 1996, the first series of Big Cat Diary was broadcast on BBC One.\n- In 1996, Keith Scholey developed and jointly produced the first series of Big Cat Diary.\n- After working on Big Cat Diary, Keith Scholey went on to become Head of the BBC Natural History Unit.\n- Bears is a 2014 nature documentary film about a family of brown bears living in the coastal mountain ranges of Alaska.\n- Aliens of the Deep was produced by Walden Media and Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Keith Scholey co-directed African Cats and Bears with Alastair Fothergill for Disneynature.",
